t)}\n  542 |         autoLoad\n  543 |       />","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\physics\\page.tsx:541:39\n  539 |         maxLevel={levelsRef.current.length > 0 ? Math.max(...levelsRef.current) : 1}\n  540 |         maxStreak={maxStreakRef.current}\n> 541 |         difficulty={levelToDifficulty(levelRef.current)}\n      |                                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Passing a ref to a function may read its value during render\n  542 |         autoLoad\n  543 |       />\n  544 |       <div className=\"flex gap-3 mt-3\">","React Hook useEffect has a missing dependency: 'runCode'. Either include it or remove the dependency array.",["2756"],"'isEasy' is assigned a value but never used.","'isMedium' is assigned a value but never used.","Error: Cannot access variable before it is declared\n\n`nextQ` is accessed before it is declared, which prevents the earlier access from updating when this value changes over time.\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\programming\\page.tsx:488:43\n  486 |         tStartRef.current = now;\n  487 |         streakRef.current = 0;\n> 488 |         advRef.current = setTimeout(() => nextQ(idx + 1), 1500);\n      |                                           ^^^^^ `nextQ` accessed before it is declared\n  489 |       }\n  490 |     }, 100);\n  491 |     tStartRef.current = Date.now();\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\programming\\page.tsx:446:3\n  444 |   };\n  445 |\n> 446 |   const nextQ = useCallback((idx: number) => {\n      |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 447 |     if (idx >= TOTAL_Q) {\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 448 |       const avgLevel = levelsRef.current.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / levelsRef.current.length;\n      …\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 492 |   // eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/exhaustive-deps\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 493 |   }, [onFinish]);\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `nextQ` is declared here\n  494 |\n  495 |   const start = () => {\n  496 |     clear();",{"range":"2757","text":"2720"},{"range":"2758","text":"2720"},"Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\programming\\page.tsx:588:85\n  586 |       <div className=\"text-6xl mb-4\">{result.correct >= 8 ? \"🏆\" : result.correct >= 5 ? \"⭐\" : \"💪\"}</div>\n  587 |       <h3 className=\"text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2\">{result.correct}/{TOTAL_Q} صحيح</h3>\n> 588 |       <p className=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mb-4\">أعلى مستوى وصلت له: Lv.{Math.max(...levelsRef.current)}</p>\n      |                                                                                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render\n  589 |       \n  590 |       <div className=\"rounded-2xl p-5 my-6 bg-indigo-50 dark:bg-indigo-950/20 border border-indigo-200/50\">\n  591 |         <div className=\"text-xs font-bold text-indigo-600 mb-1\">نقاط الجلسة المكتسبة</div>","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\programming\\page.tsx:600:22\n  598 |         correctAnswers={result.correct}\n  599 |         totalQuestions={TOTAL_Q}\n> 600 |         totalTimeMs={totalMsRef.current}\n      |                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render\n  601 |         maxLevel={levelsRef.current.length > 0 ? Math.max(...levelsRef.current) : 1}\n  602 |         maxStreak={maxStreakRef.current}\n  603 |         difficulty={levelToDifficulty(levelRef.current)}","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\programming\\page.tsx:601:19\n  599 |         totalQuestions={TOTAL_Q}\n  600 |         totalTimeMs={totalMsRef.current}\n> 601 |         maxLevel={levelsRef.current.length > 0 ? Math.max(...levelsRef.current) : 1}\n      |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render\n  602 |         maxStreak={maxStreakRef.current}\n  603 |         difficulty={levelToDifficulty(levelRef.current)}\n  604 |         autoLoad","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\programming\\page.tsx:601:62\n  599 |         totalQuestions={TOTAL_Q}\n  600 |         totalTimeMs={totalMsRef.current}\n> 601 |         maxLevel={levelsRef.current.length > 0 ? Math.max(...levelsRef.current) : 1}\n      |                                                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Passing a ref to a function may read its value during render\n  602 |         maxStreak={maxStreakRef.current}\n  603 |         difficulty={levelToDifficulty(levelRef.current)}\n  604 |         autoLoad","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\programming\\page.tsx:602:20\n  600 |         totalTimeMs={totalMsRef.current}\n  601 |         maxLevel={levelsRef.current.length > 0 ? Math.max(...levelsRef.current) : 1}\n> 602 |         maxStreak={maxStreakRef.current}\n      |                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render\n  603 |         difficulty={levelToDifficulty(levelRef.current)}\n  604 |         autoLoad\n  605 |       />","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\environments\\programming\\page.tsx:603:39\n  601 |         maxLevel={levelsRef.current.length > 0 ? Math.max(...levelsRef.current) : 1}\n  602 |         maxStreak={maxStreakRef.current}\n> 603 |         difficulty={levelToDifficulty(levelRef.current)}\n      |                                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Passing a ref to a function may read its value during render\n  604 |         autoLoad\n  605 |       />\n  606 |       ","'staggerContainerVariants' is defined but never used.",["2759"],"'staggerItemVariants' is defined but never used.",["2760"],"Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\library\\page.tsx:99:5\n   97 |   useEffect(() => {\n   98 |     sessionStorage.removeItem(\"library-refresh\");\n>  99 |     loadLibrary();\n      |     ^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  100 |   }, [loadLibrary]);\n  101 |\n  102 |   const totalVideos = courses.reduce(","'totalVideos' is assigned a value but never used.","'totalQuizzes' is assigned a value but never used.","Error: Cannot call impure function during render\n\n`Date.now` is an impure function. Calling an impure function can produce unstable results that update unpredictably when the component happens to re-render. (https://react.dev/reference/rules/components-and-hooks-must-be-pure#components-and-hooks-must-be-idempotent).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\(clerk)\\library\\page.tsx:436:45\n  434 |                     {Array.from({ length: 7 }).map((_, i) => {\n  435 |                       const dayLetters = [\"ح\", \"ن\", \"ث\", \"ر\", \"خ\", \"ج\", \"س\"]; // Sun..Sat\n> 436 |                       const date = new Date(Date.now() - (6 - i) * 86400000);\n      |                                             ^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot call impure function\n  437 |                       const isToday = i === 6;\n  438 |                       const active = stats?.weekActive?.[i] ?? false;\n  439 |                       return (","'Plus' is defined but never used.",["2761"],"'Clock' is defined but never used.",["2762"],"'XCircle' is defined but never used.",["2763"],"'teachers' is assigned a value but never used.","'loading' is assigned a value but never used.","React Hook useEffect has a missing dependency: 'fetchTeachers'. Either include it or remove the dependency array.",["2764"],["2765","2766"],["2767","2768"],["2769","2770"],["2771","2772"],"@next/next/no-img-element","Using `<img>` could result in slower LCP and higher bandwidth. Consider using `<Image />` from `next/image` or a custom image loader to automatically optimize images. This may incur additional usage or cost from your provider. See: https://nextjs.org/docs/messages/no-img-element","JSXOpeningElement",["2773","2774","2775","2776"],["2777","2778","2779","2780"],"'e' is defined but never used.","'req' is defined but never used.",["2781","2782"],"'MIN_QUESTIONS' is assigned a value but never used.","'MAX_OPTIONS' is assigned a value but never used.",["2783","2784"],["2785"],"'error' is defined but never used.",["2786","2787"],["2788","2789"],["2790","2791"],["2792"],["2793","2794"],["2795"],["2796","2797"],["2798"],["2799","2800"],["2801"],["2802","2803"],["2804"],["2805","2806"],["2807"],"'_ca' is assigned a value but never used.",["2808","2809"],["2810"],["2811","2812"],["2813"],["2814","2815"],["2816"],["2817","2818"],["2819"],["2820","2821"],["2822"],["2823","2824"],["2825"],["2826","2827"],["2828"],["2829","2830"],["2831"],["2832","2833"],"'getStudentSession' is defined but never used.",["2834"],["2835"],["2836"],["2837"],["2838"],["2839","2840"],["2841","2842"],"Error: Cannot call impure function during render\n\n`Date.now` is an impure function. Calling an impure function can produce unstable results that update unpredictably when the component happens to re-render. (https://react.dev/reference/rules/components-and-hooks-must-be-pure#components-and-hooks-must-be-idempotent).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\courses\\[id]\\learn\\page.tsx:238:34\n  236 |   const [elapsedSeconds, setElapsedSeconds] = useState(0);\n  237 |   const [completing, setCompleting] = useState(false);\n> 238 |   const [now, setNow] = useState(Date.now());\n      |                                  ^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot call impure function\n  239 |\n  240 |   // Watch modal\n  241 |   const [modalVideo, setModalVideo] = useState<{ id: string; title: string } | null>(null);","'fetchingPosition' is assigned a value but never used.","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\courses\\[id]\\learn\\page.tsx:358:40\n  356 |   }, []);\n  357 |\n> 358 |   useEffect(() => { if (courseId) void loadCourse(); }, [courseId, loadCourse]);\n      |                                        ^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  359 |\n  360 |   // Fetch saved resume position when selecting a video\n  361 |   useEffect(() => {","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\courses\\[id]\\learn\\page.tsx:363:5\n  361 |   useEffect(() => {\n  362 |     if (!activeVideoId) return;\n> 363 |     setSavedPosition(0);\n      |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  364 |     setFetchingPosition(true);\n  365 |     fetch(`/api/videos/${activeVideoId}/position`, { credentials: \"include\" })\n  366 |       .then((r) => (r.ok ? r.json() : null))","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\courses\\[id]\\learn\\page.tsx:376:5\n  374 |   // Fetch questions for active video\n  375 |   useEffect(() => {\n> 376 |     setFiredQuestionIds(new Set());\n      |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  377 |     setActiveQuestion(null);\n  378 |     setActiveOverlayQuestion(null);\n  379 |     if (!player?.videoId) {","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\courses\\[id]\\learn\\page.tsx:430:20\n  428 |\n  429 |   useEffect(() => {\n> 430 |     if (!player) { setElapsedSeconds(0); return; }\n      |                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  431 |     const tick = () => {\n  432 |       setElapsedSeconds(Math.floor((Date.now() - new Date(player.startedAt).getTime()) / 1000));\n  433 |     };","Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\nJ:\\crispy-octo-doodle-1\\src\\app\\courses\\[id]\\learn\\page.tsx:901:44\n  899 |                             videoId={player!.videoId}\n  900 |                             watchSessionId={player!.watchSessionId}\n> 901 |                             currentSecond={playerTimeRef.current}\n      |                                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot access ref value during render\n  902 |                             onAnswered={handleQuestionAnswered}\n  903 |                      